ental diff that only indexes new/changed directories and drops gone ones. The plan does not state that the temporary database is seeded with the unchanged entries before the rename; if it contains only the diff, the atomic whole-file replacement would discard every unchanged ticket's index rows.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2544ce5a67778aad","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Concurrent writers and Persistence and freshness","norm_id":"na1415920b29af149","priority":0.6667,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A changed ticket triggers reconciliation; the temp DB is built from only the diff; os.rename replaces the live file; all previously-indexed unchanged tickets vanish from results until the next change re-triggers a build","Two reconcilers each handle a different changed ticket; the loser's rename clobbers the winner's, and neither temp DB holds the other's change"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify that reconciliation copies the current index into the temporary database (or opens it from a copy), applies the new/changed/dropped diff to that copy, then os.rename-swaps it in — so the atomic replacement never loses unchanged entries while remaining incremental on the warm path.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["7 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable).","vague/subjective terms present: better"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State where the `alias` result field is sourced (persisted in the index vs looked up from the ticket store at query time).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.534,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: 'Each result carries `id`, `alias`, `title` and `score`.'","Ranking section only names 'title and description' and 'id', 'score' — alias provenance is absent","E2 signal (1)/(2): a referenced output field with no stated source is a data-design ambiguity"],"finding":"The result shape includes an `alias` field, but the Ranking section (and persistence section) only describe indexing title and description and never state where `alias` is sourced or stored. An executor cannot populate `alias` without a stated provenance (ticket metadata lookup vs persisted in the index).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe60c91d7dc565f8b","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria ('Each result carries `id`, `alias`, `title` and `score`') vs Approach/Ranking","norm_id":"ndad742e0108dc2d4","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor builds the index persisting only title/description and must decide at query time where alias comes from"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to the Persistence section stating that each indexed row persists the ticket id, alias, and title alongside the FTS text, and that query results read alias from that row.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify os.replace (not os.rename) for the live-file swap so the atomic-overwrite works on Windows as well as POSIX.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'Reconciliation builds into a temporary database in the same directory and replaces the live file with `os.rename`, atomic within a filesystem.'","On Windows, os.rename raises FileExistsError if the target path exists, whereas POSIX os.rename atomically overwrites; os.replace is the cross-platform atomic-overwrite call."],"finding":"The reconciliation step relies on os.rename to replace the live index file, which on Windows raises when the destination already exists (unlike POSIX overwrite semantics); the second and subsequent reconciliations would fail to replace an existing index.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f78901d6c2ded60ba","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Concurrent writers: \"replaces the live file with `os.rename`, atomic within a filesystem\"","norm_id":"n2141c04cdfe4b77f","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Platform=Windows, developer workstation: the first build creates the index, but every subsequent reconciliation (changed/new/removed ticket) fails at os.rename because the live file exists; the failure is swallowed to an empty result and logged at warning, so the index silently stops reflecting store changes on Windows."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace the live index via `os.replace(tmp, live)`, which performs an atomic overwrite on both POSIX and Windows, and note this in the Concurrent writers section.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius